message: "If you use House Party Protocol, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "House Party Protocol"
abstract: "House Party Protocol (HPP) is a local-first harness for coding agents. It sits around the work an agent does in Claude Code or Codex CLI and turns four questions into executable contracts: what may run, who may approve, what counts as proof, and where the next step comes from after an interruption."
version: "2.4.2"
date-released: "2026-09-21"
